UBERON:0002514 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "intramembranous bone" ;
    IAO:0000115 "Bone tissue forms directly within mesenchyme, and does not replace other tissues[TAO]. Intramembranous ossification is the formation of bone in which osteoblasts secrete a collagen-proteoglycan matrix that binds calcium salts and becomes calcified[GO]. Intramembranous ossification is the way flat bones and the shell of a turtle are formed[GO]. Unlike endochondral ossification, cartilage is not present during intramembranous ossification[WP]." ;
    OboInOwl:hasDbXref "EMAPA:36615",
        "TAO:0001644",
        "Wikipedia:Intramembranous_ossification",
        "ZFA:0001635" ;
