TARA:2976260 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "SI 15" ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "[Acupoint Location, Pinyin Label, Chinese Label] WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization (WHO), WHO Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 95. https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/353407",
        "[Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, Indications] Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Edited by C. Xinnong, Rev. Ed., Foreign Languages Press, Beijing, China, 1999. Ch. 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridians. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7." ;
    tara-ap:hasChineseLabel "肩中兪(俞)" ;
    tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation UBERON:0008231 ;
    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "Superficially, the medial cutaneous branches of the posterior rami of the first and second thoracic nerves, the accessory nerve; deeper, the dorsal scapular nerve." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription """In the upper back region, at the same level as the inferior border of the spinous process of the seventh cervical vertebra (C7), 2 B-cun lateral to the posterior median line.
 - Note: SI 15 is located at the intersection of two imaginary lines: the vertical line of the junction of the lateral one third and the medial two thirds of the line connecting the posterior median line with the medial border of the scapula and the horizontal line inferior to the spinous process of the seventh cervical vertebra (C7).""" ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture obliquely 0.3-0.6 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
    tara-ap:hasPinyinLabel "Jianzhongshu" ;
