    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "aphasia",
        "apoplexy",
        "deafness",
        "epilepsy",
        "mental disorder",
        "muteness",
        "neck rigidity",
        "occipital headache",
        "stiffness of the tongue",
        "sudden hoarseness of the voice" ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription """In the posterior region of the neck, in the depression superior to the spinous process of the second cervical vertebra (C2), on the posterior median line.
 - Note: After locating GV 16, GV 15 is located 0.5 B-cun inferior to GV 16.""" ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-0.8 inch. Neither upward obliquely nor deep puncture is advisable. It is near the medullary bulb in the deep layer, and the depth and angle of the puncture should be paid strict attention to." ;
