TARA:6119170 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Extra Acupuncture Meridian"@en ;
    IAO:0000115 "A Meridian, other than the twelve principal meridians, that is not directly affiliated with a zang or fu organ system and does not stand in an exterior-interior pairing with another meridian."@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Edited by C. Xinnong, Rev. Ed., Foreign Languages Press, Beijing, China, 1999. Ch. 5, Sec. III, The Eight Extra Meridians, Page 82. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7." ;
    dcterms:description "Represents the extra meridians. The eight extra meridians are the Governor Vessel, Conception Vessel, Thoroughfare Vessel, Belt Vessel, Yang Heel Vessel, Yin Heel Vessel, Yang Link Vessel and Yin Link Vessel. They are different from the twelve main meridians because none of them pertains to the zang organs and communicates with the fu organs of pertains to the fu organs and communicates with the zang organs. And they are not exteriorly-interiorly related. Apart from the Governor Vessel and Conception Vessel which have their own acupuncture points, the extra meridians share their points with other main meridians."@en ;
    tara-ap:hasSynonym "Extra Acupoint Meridian",
        "Extra Meridian" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf TARA:7226516 .

TARA:6135195 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "GV 17" ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "[Acupoint Location, Pinyin Label, Chinese Label] WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization (WHO), WHO Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 212. https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/353407",
        "[Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, Indications] Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Edited by C. Xinnong, Rev. Ed., Foreign Languages Press, Beijing, China, 1999. Ch. 10, Acupuncture Points of the Governor and the Conception Vessels and the Extra Points. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7." ;
    tara-ap:hasChineseLabel "腦(脑,脳)戶" ;
    tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation UBERON:0000033 ;
    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "The branch of the great occipital nerve." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "dizziness",
        "epilepsy",
        "pain in the neck",
        "stiffness of the neck" ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription """On the head, in the depression superior to the external occipital protuberance.
 - Note: GV 17 is located in the depression at the intersection of two imaginary lines: the vertical line of the posterior median line and the horizontal line of the superior border of the external occipital protuberance, at the same level as BL 9.""" ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture subcutaneously 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
    tara-ap:hasPinyinLabel "Naohu" ;
    tara-ap:hasSpecificReferenceLocation UBERON:0013469,
        ILX:0795312 ;
    tara-ap:hasSynonym "Du 17",
        "Governor Vessel 17",
        "VG 17" ;
    tara-ap:hasVasculatureInformation "The branches of the occipital arteries and veins of the both sides." ;
    tara-ap:isLocatedOnMeridian TARA:0386099 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:intersectionOf ( TARA:5151019 [ a owl:Restriction ;
