tara-ap:hasMeridianAnnotationProperty a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Meridian Annotation Property"@en ;
    IAO:0000112 "This grouping property is never meant to be used for direct annotations. Direct annotations must be asserted through its specific subproperties."@en ;
    dcterms:description "An annotation property that groups all meridian-specific annotation properties in TARA Acupoints Ontology. Therefore, the domain for each of its sub-properties is specified as 'Acupuncture Meridan'."@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:topTARAAnnotaionProperty .

tara-ap:hasRelatedArtery a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Nearby Artery"@en ;
    IAO:0000112 """The acupoint 'LU 1' has the following vasculature information:
- "Superolaterally, the axillary artery and vein, the thoracoacromial artery and vein."

Based on the information above, we can state:
- 'LU 1' tara-ap:hasRelatedArtery 'axillary artery'.
- 'LU 1' tara-ap:hasRelatedArtery 'thoraco-acromial artery'."""@en ;
    dcterms:description """An annotation property that records the IRI of a specific artery in the vicinity of an acupoint's penetrated region (relevant to safe needling). 
- Corresponds to the object property tara-op:hasRelatedArtery, which is used for logical axioms."""@en ;
    dcterms:references tara-op:hasRelatedArtery ;
    dcterms:requires tara-ap:hasVasculatureInformation ;
    tara-ap:hasSynonym "Related Artery"@en ;
    rdfs:domain TARA:1132428 ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy tara-ap:hasVasculatureInformation ;
    rdfs:range UBERON:0001062 ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:hasRelatedVasculature .

tara-ap:hasRelatedNerve a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Related Nerve"@en ;
    IAO:0000112 """The acupoint 'LU 1' has the following innervation information: 
- "The intermediate supraclavicular nerve, the branches of the anterior thoracic nerve, and the lateral cutaneous branch of the first intercostal nerve."

Based on the information above, we can state:
- 'LU 1' tara-ap:hasRelatedNerve 'Intermediate Supraclavicular Nerve'.
- 'LU 1' tara-ap:hasRelatedNerve 'medial pectoral nerve'.
- 'LU 1' tara-ap:hasRelatedNerve 'First intercostal nerve'.

Note: The medial pectoral nerve (also known as the medial anterior thoracic nerve) is (typically) a branch of the medial cord of the brachial plexus and is derived from ventral rami  C8-T1."""@en ;
    dcterms:description """An annotation property that records the IRI of a nerve within the vicinity of an acupoint's location, asserting that a specific named nerve, nerve trunk, or branch physically occupies or passes through the three-dimensional tissue volume penetrated by the acupoint needle.
- Corresponds to the object property tara-op:hasRelatedNerve, which is used for logical axioms."""@en ;
    dcterms:references tara-op:hasRelatedNerve ;
    dcterms:requires tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation ;
    rdfs:domain TARA:1132428 ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation ;
    rdfs:range UBERON:0001062 ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:hasRelatedInnervation .

tara-ap:hasRelatedVein a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Nearby Vein"@en ;
    IAO:0000112 """The acupoint 'LU 1' has the following vasculature information:
- "Superolaterally, the axillary artery and vein, the thoracoacromial artery and vein."

Based on the information above, we can state:
- 'LU 1' tara-ap:hasRelatedVein 'axillary vein'.
- 'LU 1' tara-ap:hasRelatedVein 'thoracoacromial vein'."""@en ;
    dcterms:description """An annotation property that records the IRI of a specific vein in the vicinity of an acupoint's penetrated region (relevant to safe needling).
- Corresponds to the object property tara-op:hasRelatedVein, which is used for logical axioms."""@en ;
    dcterms:references tara-op:hasRelatedVein ;
    dcterms:requires tara-ap:hasVasculatureInformation ;
    tara-ap:hasSynonym "Related Vein"@en ;
    rdfs:domain TARA:1132428 ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy tara-ap:hasVasculatureInformation ;
    rdfs:range UBERON:0001062 ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:hasRelatedVasculature .

tara-ap:hasSpecificReferenceLocation a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Reference Location"@en ;
    IAO:0000112 """The acupoint 'LU 1' has the following locational description:
- "On the anterior thoracic region, at the same level as the first intercostal space, lateral to the infraclavicular fossa, 6 B-cun lateral to the anterior median line."

Based on the description above, 'LU 1' has three specific reference locations within the general surface of 'Anterior Thoracic Region'. So, using this property's superproperty, hasGeneralSurfaceLocation, we can state:
- 'LU 1' tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation 'Anterior Thoracic Region'.

After stating the general location, we can use this property to assert the specific reference locations:
- 'LU 1' tara-ap:hasSpecificReferenceLocation 'Infraclavicular Fossa' .
- 'LU 1' tara-ap:hasSpecificReferenceLocation 'First Intercostal Space' .
- 'LU 1' tara-ap:hasSpecificReferenceLocation  'Anterior Median Line' ."""@en ;
    dcterms:description """An annotation property that records the IRI of a specific anatomical landmark within the general surface region of an acupoint (using UBERON or ILX IRI).
- Corresponds to the object property tara-op:hasSpecificReferenceLocation, which is used for logical axioms."""@en ;
    dcterms:references tara-op:hasSpecificReferenceLocation ;
    dcterms:requires tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription ;
    tara-ap:hasSynonym "Specific Reference Location"@en ;
    rdfs:domain TARA:1132428 ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription ;
    rdfs:range UBERON:0001062 ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation .

tara-ap:topTARAAnnotaionProperty a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "tara:topAnnotationProperty"@en ;
    dcterms:description "An annotation property that groups all TARA-specific annotation properties. It is a grouping relation that functions purely as an organizational root for browsing/querying the TARA-specific annotation property tree."@en .

tara-kb:hasMeridianObjectProperty a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    IAO:0000112 "This grouping property is never meant to be used for direct assertion of axioms. Direct axioms must be asserted through its specific, leaf-level subproperties." ;
    dcterms:description "An object property grouping all meridian-specific object properties in TARA Acupoints Ontology. Therefore, the domain for this property is 'Acupuncture Meridian' which is inherited by all its subproperties." ;
    rdfs:domain TARA:7226516 ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-op:topTARAObjectProperty .

tara-op:topTARAObjectProperty a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "tara-op:topObjectProperty" ;
    IAO:0000112 "This grouping property is never meant to be used for direct assertion of axioms. Direct axioms must be asserted through its specific, leaf-level subproperties." ;
    dcterms:description "A grouping relation that functions purely as an organizational root for browsing/querying the TARA-specific object property tree, and asserts no independent semantic commitment that a reasoner needs to satisfy."@en .

BFO:0000001 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "entity" ;
    IAO:0000115 "An entity is anything that exists or has existed or will exist." ;
    IAO:0000116 "'Entity' is a primitive term: it is so basic to our understanding of reality that there is no way of defining it non-circularly, so BFO supplies only an elucidation rather than a genus-differentia definition. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [001-001])" ;
    IAO:0000119 "BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021), axiom [001-001]." ;
    IAO:0000412 obo:bfo.owl ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy obo:bfo.owl .

BFO:0000016 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "disposition" ;
    IAO:0000112 "the cell wall is disposed to filter chemicals in endocytosis and exocytosis; certain people have a predisposition to colon cancer; children are innately disposed to categorize objects in certain ways." ;
    IAO:0000115 "(Elucidation) b is a disposition means: b is a realizable entity & b’s bearer is some material entity & b is such that if it ceases to exist, then its bearer is physically changed, & b’s realization occurs when and because this bearer is in some special physical circumstances, & this realization occurs in virtue of the bearer’s physical make-up. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [062-002])" ;
    IAO:0000119 "BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021)." ;
    IAO:0000412 obo:bfo.owl ;
    rdfs:subClassOf BFO:0000017 ;
    owl:disjointWith BFO:0000023 .

BFO:0000019 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "quality" ;
    IAO:0000112 "the mass of this piece of gold; the length of the circumference of your waist; the shape of your nose." ;
    IAO:0000115 "(Elucidation) a quality is a specifically dependent continuant that, in contrast to roles and dispositions, does not require any further process in order to be realized. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [055-001])" ;
    IAO:0000119 "BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021)." ;
    IAO:0000412 obo:bfo.owl ;
    rdfs:subClassOf BFO:0000020 .

BFO:0000031 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "generically dependent continuant" ;
    IAO:0000115 "b is a generically dependent continuant = Def. b is a continuant that g-depends_on one or more other entities."@en ;
    IAO:0000116 "Included as a bare stub solely to carry disjointWith axioms against BFO:0000004 and BFO:0000020, the two other direct subclasses of continuant; not independently used as a TARA class." ;
    IAO:0000119 "BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021), axiom [074-001]." ;
    IAO:0000412 obo:bfo.owl ;
    rdfs:comment "A continuant that is dependent on one or other independent continuant bearers. For every instance of A requires some instance of (an independent continuant type) B but which instance of B serves can change from time to time."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy obo:bfo.owl ;
    rdfs:subClassOf BFO:0000002 .

BFO:0000034 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "function" ;
    IAO:0000112 "the function of a hammer to drive in nails; the function of a heart pacemaker to regulate the beating of a heart through electricity; the function of amylase in saliva to break down starch into sugar;" ;
    IAO:0000115 "(Elucidation) A function is a disposition that exists in virtue of the bearer’s physical make-up and this physical make-up is something the bearer possesses because it came into being, either through evolution (in the case of natural biological entities) or through intentional design (in the case of artifacts), in order to realize processes of a certain sort. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [064-001])" ;
    IAO:0000119 "BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021)." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf BFO:0000016 .

RO:0000087 a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has role"@en ;
    IAO:0000112 "This person has role this investigator role. LU1 hasSpecialPointRole Front-Mu Point of the Lung Role." ;
    IAO:0000115 "A relation between an independent continuant (the bearer) and a role, in which the role specifically depends on the bearer for its existence." ;
    IAO:0000116 "A bearer can have many roles, and its roles can exist for different periods of time, but none of its roles can exist when the bearer does not exist. A role need not be realized at all the times that the role exists."@en ;
    IAO:0000118 "has_role"@en ;
    IAO:0000119 "OBO Relations Ontology (RO), http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl." ;
    IAO:0000412 obo:ro.owl ;
    rdfs:domain BFO:0000004 ;
    rdfs:range BFO:0000023 ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf RO:0000053 .

RO:0002131 a owl:ObjectProperty,
        owl:SymmetricProperty ;
    rdfs:label "overlaps" ;
    IAO:0000112 "LU1 hasRelatedSubSurfaceAnatomy Axillary Artery." ;
    IAO:0000115 "x overlaps y if and only if there exists some z such that x has part z and z part of y." ;
    IAO:0000116 "part_of (BFO:0000050) is itself a subproperty of overlaps in RO's own hierarchy (is_a: RO:0002131 overlaps), since anything that is part_of something automatically overlaps it -- this is why overlaps, not part_of, is the true root of this branch." ;
    IAO:0000119 "OBO Relations Ontology (RO), http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl." ;
    IAO:0000412 obo:ro.owl ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-op:roObjectProperty .

UBERON:0000013 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "sympathetic nervous system" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The sympathetic nervous system is one of the two divisions of the vertebrate autonomic nervous system (the other being the parasympathetic nervous system). The sympathetic preganglionic neurons have their cell bodies in the thoracic and lumbar regions of the spinal cord and connect to the paravertebral chain of sympathetic ganglia. Innervate heart and blood vessels, sweat glands, viscera and the adrenal medulla. Most sympathetic neurons, but not all, use noradrenaline as a post-ganglionic neurotransmitter [GO]." ;
    OboInOwl:hasDbXref "AAO:0010487",
        "BIRNLEX:2516",
        "BTO:0001832",
        "CALOHA:TS-2050",
        "EFO:0000893",
