            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0001404 ],
        UBERON:0001637 .

rdfs:label a owl:AnnotationProperty .

BFO:0000002 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "continuant" ;
    IAO:0000112 "An organism; a heart; a color; a role; the sequence of a protein molecule." ;
    IAO:0000115 "An entity that exists in full at any time in which it exists at all, persists through time while maintaining its identity and has no temporal parts."@en ;
    IAO:0000119 "BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021)." ;
    IAO:0000412 obo:bfo.owl ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy obo:bfo.owl ;
    rdfs:subClassOf BFO:0000001 ;
    owl:disjointWith [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom BFO:0000003 ],
        BFO:0000003 .

BFO:0000003 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "occurrent" ;
    IAO:0000115 "(Elucidation) an occurrent is an entity that unfolds itself in time or it is the instantaneous boundary of such an entity (for example a beginning or an ending) or it is a temporal or spatiotemporal region which such an entity occupies_temporal_region or occupies_spatiotemporal_region. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [077-002])"@en ;
    IAO:0000119 "BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021)." ;
    IAO:0000412 obo:bfo.owl ;
    rdfs:subClassOf BFO:0000001 ;
    owl:disjointWith [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom BFO:0000002 ] .

BFO:0000020 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "specifically dependent continuant" ;
    IAO:0000112 "A color; a shape; a role; a disposition." ;
    IAO:0000115 "b is a specifically dependent continuant = Def. b is a continuant & there is some independent continuant c which is not a spatial region and which is such that b s-depends_on c at every time t during the course of b’s existence. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [050-003])"@en ;
    IAO:0000119 "BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021)." ;
    IAO:0000412 obo:bfo.owl ;
    rdfs:comment "A continuant that inheres in or is borne by other entities. Every instance of A requires some specific instance of B which must always be the same."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf BFO:0000002 ;
    owl:disjointWith BFO:0000031 .

BFO:0000023 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "role" ;
    IAO:0000112 "The priest role; the student role; the role of subject in a clinical trial; the role of a stone in marking a property boundary; the role of a building in serving as a military target." ;
    IAO:0000115 "(Elucidation) A role is a realizable entity that exists because there is some single bearer that is in some special physical, social, or institutional set of circumstances in which this bearer does not have to be, and is not such that, if it ceases to exist, then the physical make-up of the bearer is thereby changed.",
        "A realizable entity  the manifestation of which brings about some result or end that is not essential to a continuant  in virtue of the kind of thing that it is but that can be served or participated in by that kind of continuant  in some kinds of natural, social or institutional contexts."@en ;
    IAO:0000119 "BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021)." ;
    IAO:0000412 obo:bfo.owl ;
    rdfs:subClassOf BFO:0000017 .

BFO:0000040 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "material entity" ;
    IAO:0000112 "An organism; a heart; a chair; a lung; an apple." ;
    IAO:0000115 "An independent continuant that is spatially extended whose identity is independent of that of other entities and can be maintained through time."@en ;
    IAO:0000119 "BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2:2021)." ;
    IAO:0000412 obo:bfo.owl,
        obo:uberon.owl ;
    rdfs:subClassOf BFO:0000004 ;
    owl:disjointWith BFO:0000141 .

RO:0000052 a owl:FunctionalProperty,
        owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "characteristic of"@en ;
    IAO:0000111 "characteristic of",
        "inheres in"@en ;
    IAO:0000112 "This red color inheres in this apple. This fragility inheres in this vase.",
        "this fragility is a characteristic of this vase"@en,
        "this red color is a characteristic of this apple"@en ;
    IAO:0000115 "A relation between a specifically dependent continuant (the characteristic) and any other entity (the bearer), in which the characteristic depends on the bearer for its existence.",
        "a relation between a specifically dependent continuant (the characteristic) and any other entity (the bearer), in which the characteristic depends on the bearer for its existence."@en ;
    IAO:0000116 "IMPORTANT: RO renamed this term's preferred label from 'inheres in' to 'characteristic of' in its 2021-03-08 release, and correspondingly relaxed its definition (the bearer need no longer be an independent continuant). BFO 2020 retains a separate, more restricted native relation, BFO:0000197 (inheres in), for the classic independent-continuant-bearer case. TARA's tara-op:isSpecialPointDesignationOf (reserved, not currently populated) was originally modeled against the older, narrower 'inheres in' reading of this ID; if that reserved property is ever activated, switching its superproperty to BFO:0000197 would better match current upstream terminology." ;
    IAO:0000118 "inheres_in"@en ;
    IAO:0000119 "OBO Relations Ontology (RO) core.obo, RO:0000052 'characteristic of' (formerly 'inheres in')." ;
    IAO:0000412 obo:ro.owl ;
    rdfs:comment "Note that this relation was previously called \"inheres in\", but was changed to be called \"characteristic of\" because BFO2 uses \"inheres in\" in a more restricted fashion. This relation differs from BFO2:inheres_in in two respects: (1) it does not impose a range constraint, and thus it allows qualities of processes, as well as of information entities, whereas BFO2 restricts inheres_in to only apply to independent continuants (2) it is declared functional, i.e. something can only be a characteristic of one thing." ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-op:roObjectProperty ;
    owl:inverseOf RO:0000053 .

