RO:0001025 a owl:ObjectProperty,
        owl:TransitiveProperty ;
    rdfs:label "located in",
        "located in"@en ;
    IAO:0000111 "located in"@en ;
    IAO:0000112 "my brain is located in my head"@en,
        "this rat is located in this cage"@en ;
    IAO:0000115 "c is located_in c1 (at a time t) if and only if the spatial region occupied by c is part_of the spatial region occupied by c1 (at t). This relation comprehends both exact location (as when a portion of fluid exactly fills a cavity) and inexact/containment-style location (as between brain and head, or ovum and uterus)." ;
    IAO:0000116 "Chosen over overlaps (RO:0002131) for the Acupoint surface-anatomy and meridian relations because located_in does not require the two related continuants to be of the same BFO category (material vs. immaterial), unlike overlaps, which requires a literal shared part. The property-chain axiom (located_in o part_of -> located_in) means that if c is located_in c1 and c1 is part_of c2, then c is automatically inferred located_in c2 as well.",
        "Location as a relation between instances: The primitive instance-level relation c located_in r at t reflects the fact that each continuant is at any given time associated with exactly one spatial region, namely its exact location. Following we can use this relation to define a further instance-level location relation - not between a continuant and the region which it exactly occupies, but rather between one continuant and another. c is located in c1, in this sense, whenever the spatial region occupied by c is part_of the spatial region occupied by c1.    Note that this relation comprehends both the relation of exact location between one continuant and another which obtains when r and r1 are identical (for example, when a portion of fluid exactly fills a cavity), as well as those sorts of inexact location relations which obtain, for example, between brain and head or between ovum and uterus"@en,
        "Most location relations will only hold at certain times, but this is difficult to specify in OWL. See http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro/docs/temporal-semantics/"@en ;
    IAO:0000118 "located_in"@en ;
    IAO:0000119 "OBO Relations Ontology (RO), http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl." ;
    IAO:0000412 obo:ro.owl ;
    dcterms:source "http://www.obofoundry.org/ro/#OBO_REL:located_in" ;
    rdfs:domain [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:intersectionOf ( BFO:0000004 [ a owl:Class ;
                        owl:complementOf BFO:0000006 ] ) ],
        BFO:0000004 ;
    rdfs:range [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:intersectionOf ( BFO:0000004 [ a owl:Class ;
                        owl:complementOf BFO:0000006 ] ) ],
        BFO:0000004 ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-op:roObjectProperty ;
    owl:propertyChainAxiom ( RO:0001025 partOf: ) .

