ILX:0795334 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "palmar wrist crease" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The palmar wrist crease is the transverse skin fold that appears on the palm side of the wrist when the hand is flexed. It marks the boundary between the forearm and the palm and is located approximately at the level of the distal radius and ulna." ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795334 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0019243 .

UBERON:0000916 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "abdomen" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The subdivision of the vertebrate body between the thorax and pelvis. The ventral part of the abdomen contains the abdominal cavity and visceral organs. The dorsal part includes the abdominal section of the vertebral column." ;
    IAO:0000116 "Vertebrate specific. In arthropods 'abdomen' is the most distal section of the body which lies behind the thorax or cephalothorax. If need be we can introduce some grouping class" ;
